  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong upward trend (e.g., >85 EUR) followed by high sentiment scores (>0.20), the model systematically overestimates future prices by ignoring immediate mean reversion risks.",
    "The model exhibits significant lag in detecting sudden volatility spikes; when true outcomes jump >10% from recent lows, the forecast remains anchored to the previous trend line instead of pivoting upward.",
    "In periods of high sentiment (0.25+), the model fails to account for 'sell-off' corrections that occur within the first 7 days of the forecast horizon, resulting in a consistent downward bias relative to actual early-period outcomes.",
    "The model assumes linear extrapolation during volatile regimes but true outcomes display high-frequency oscillation; forecasts should be adjusted with a volatility buffer when sentiment history shows mixed signals (0.00 alternating with 0.20+).",
    "When the last 3 days of history are above 85 EUR and sentiment is neutral to positive, reduce the forecasted growth rate by 40% to prevent overshooting the peak."
  ]
